index e2e7e76ab..131a82741 100644
--- a/docs/guide/spinel.md
+++ b/docs/guide/spinel.md
@@ -244,3 +244,34 @@ on, jemalloc, and Puma's default configuration — on the same machine:
 Read that page rather than a number quoted here; it changes with
 every Spinel release and the methodology is written beside the
 charts.
+
+## PostgreSQL (experimental)
+
+Select the libpq backend at emission time:
+
+```sh
+RH_DATABASE_ADAPTER=postgresql roundhouse --target spinel -o out/pg /path/to/app
+cd out/pg
+spin build
+DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost/app ./build/bin/<app>
+# Use a separate PostgreSQL database for destructive model test resets:
+DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost/app_test spin test
+```
+
+The app must ship `db/structure.sql` (a schema-only pg_dump, preferably
+`--no-owner --no-privileges`). Ship `db/schema.rb` as well for type inference,
+or use structure.sql alone. On boot, the binary acquires a transaction advisory
+lock and loads the dump only when the public schema has no tables. It does not
+run pending migrations on an existing schema. The load is transactional and
+concurrent boots serialize. psql's `\restrict`/`\unrestrict` controls are removed
+from the emitted dump; other psql commands are unsupported.
+
+Install libpq headers to build (`libpq-dev`) and libpq to run (`libpq5`).
+`DATABASE_POOL_SIZE` controls the pool (default 8); request leases and
+transactions pin a connection. UTC, ISO date style, and standard string
+literals are set on every connection. Integer/UUID inserts use RETURNING.
+Text arrays (one dimension, non-null elements) and JSONB are encoded/decoded,
+and `with_lock` joins/opens a transaction and reloads with FOR UPDATE. Nested
+transactions join; savepoints and `requires_new` are not implemented.
+
+Without the emission environment variable, SQLite remains the default.
